    "result_text": "All tests pass. The suite consists of the `AcceptanceTest` (the others are the abstract base and a helper), and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature following the app's existing Spring/OpenAPI conventions, where derived read-only fields (like `initials`, `membershipNumber`, `displayName`) are computed on the domain model and auto-mapped to the response DTO.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n   - Added an optional `title` input property (enum `MR`/`MRS`/`MS`/`DR`) to the `OwnerFields` schema.\n   - Added a read-only `salutation` property to the `Owner` schema.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 the single responsibility for composing the value lives with the owner's own data:\n   - Added a persisted `title` field (`@Column`) with getter/setter.\n   - Added `getSalutation()`, which returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is present. It reuses `getLastName()` rather than duplicating name access.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `title` column, since `ddl-auto=none` for the test (hsqldb) profile.\n\n**No mapper change was needed:** MapStruct auto-maps `salutation` from `Owner.getSalutation()` and converts the DTO `title` enum \u2194 the `String` model field in both directions, consistent with how the other derived fields are wired.\n\nThe `coreComposesSalutation` acceptance test confirms the round trip: creating an owner with `title=DR`, `lastName=who` yields `salutation` = `\"DR who\"` on read.",
